# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*~
*.swp

# built binary + Go artifacts
/gothic
/vendor/
*.test
coverage.out

# Artifacts a test run can leave behind. The hot-reload loop builds into tmp/
# and the routes codegen writes src/routes/, both relative to the working
# directory, so a test whose goroutine outlives its chdir writes them into the
# package directory instead of its temp dir. Scoped to those two packages on
# purpose: a bare tmp/ or .gothicCli/ pattern would also swallow the scaffold
# payload under internal/scaffold/, which must stay tracked because it ships
# embedded in the binary.
/internal/cmd/tmp/
/internal/cmd/src/
/internal/build/tmp/
/internal/build/src/
/internal/cmd/.gothicCli/
/internal/build/.gothicCli/
